yet read in full is marked unread.

=== IMASM guide, MoDoT/IMSCRIBERS_GUIDE_TO_IMASM.md (read in full 2026-08-30) ===

Alphabet entries for the fork/fuse dyad:
  ∈  FSPLIT  fork (δ): the ONLY brancher   valence 1→2, 1→3   WORK? no
  ∋  FFUSE   fuse (μ): the ONLY merger     valence 2→1, 3→1   WORK? no

Part I: "δ cuts the register into a PARTITION, and which partition depends on
how many arms it has: {T,t} | {F,f} at two, and {T} | {F} | {t,f} at three,
the truth cut taken inside the constructive block with the non-constructive
pair held whole. Both are partitions of the four base values, so μ∘δ = id at
either arity. On the classical slice, where t and f are absent, the three-arm
cut IS the two-arm cut: the information arm carries nothing."

Part I, immediately after: "Note what this rules out: the two-arm cut is not
the three-arm cut with an arm dropped. Dropping the information arm leaves
{T} | {F}, which loses t and f and would not recover its input. They coincide
on the slice, not by truncation."

Part I: arity is forced, not chosen: "⊞ sets t and f together, so the
non-constructive pair can only ever be entered as a block, and three is what
the gate set leaves."

Part III, close condition: a program closes iff every ∈/∋ participates in an
ancestry pair AND at least one such pair carries a WORK opcode on its arms.
"Split→fuse with nothing between is μ∘δ=id, which type-checks nothing. The
close condition is μ∘δ over a TRANSFORMED object: split, work, fuse."

Part IV, the carrier: register is a SIXTEEN_3 value, subset of {T,F,t,f},
sixteen states N={} to A={T,F,t,f}. FOUR is the classical slice {T,F} of the
same carrier (Belnap B={T,F}, N={}). Three orderings each with meet/join:
  ≤_i information    x ⊆ y                                          ⊓/⊔
  ≤_t truth           x∩{T,t} ⊆ y∩{T,t} and y∩{F,f} ⊆ x∩{F,f}        ∧/∨
  ≤_c constructivity  x∩{T,F} ⊆ y∩{T,F} and y∩{t,f} ⊆ x∩{t,f}        △/▽
"Flow uses ≤_i: shuttling only ever moves values up the information order."

Part IV, gates: "FSPLIT ∈ / ∈ — δ fans the register's own partition onto its
arms: at two, truth part x∩{T,t} and falsity part x∩{F,f}; at three, x∩{T},
x∩{F}, and the information part x∩{t,f}." "FFUSE ∋ / ∋ — μ / μ₃ joins: union
of the arms."

Part V, flow: "the canonical protocol word (⊢∈≻∋⊤ as VINIT FSPLIT AFWD FFUSE
EVALT) is lossless: B splits to (T,F) and fuses back to B, the operational
split_fuse_id." Also in this part: a variant with AREV on the truth arm
"closes in structure and fails in value: fed Tf, recovered Ff, NOT id."

Part XIII, canonical words list includes:
  ⊢∈≻⊤∋⊣   lossless protocol, closes in shape and value, recovers B → T,
           wired at three arms is the same word, on the FOUR slice flows
           identically with the third arm carrying nothing
  ⊢∈⊙∋⊣    identity, reconnects with no work, μ∘δ=id → N
  ⊢∈⊙⊙⊙∋⊣  tri identity, same reading → N

Verb index includes `imasm16_3 check <word>` (tri type-check, same T/N/B/F
reading), `imasm16_3 algebra <op> A B` with ops leq_i|leq_t|leq_c|meet_t|
join_t|meet_c|join_c, `imasm eval`/`imasm eval16` for flow readouts.

=== FDEAsymptotic.lean, p4rakernel/p4ramill/Imscribing/Paraconsistent/FDEAsymptotic.lean
    (350 lines, read in full earlier this session) ===

`inductive FDEN (n : ℕ) : Type` — bilattice with n+2 truth values total:
a bottom, a top, and n middle values indexed by Fin n.

`fdenCardinality n = n + 2`.

FDE(2) proven isomorphic to Belnap FOUR: `fde2_isomorphic_to_belnap` (bijective).
FDE(3) proven isomorphic to ColorState (quark color): `fde3_isomorphic_to_color`
(bijective).

`fdeEmbed k n hkn : FDEN k → FDEN n` for k ≤ n. Proven injective:
`fdeEmbed_injective`. Proven NOT surjective for adjacent steps:
`fdeEmbed_not_surjective`. This is the only explicit map between two different
FDEN arities in the file, and it runs upward (smaller n into larger n).

General theorem: `truthValuesGrowMonotonically {k n} (hkn : k < n) :
∃ e, Injective e ∧ ¬ Surjective e` — states growth/injectivity, not a
downward or restriction map.

`inductive FDEInf` (bot / mid : ℕ / top) as a direct limit. `fdeToInf_injective`
and `fdeInf_infinite` both proven.

§7 gives a physical correspondence table: electron/SU(2)/FDE(2) →
quark/SU(3)/FDE(3) → preon/SU(4)/FDE(4) → Planck/gravity/FDE(∞).

§8: `fdeTowerImscription`, with `fdeTower_tier` proven equal to `O_inf` via
`native_decide`.

Census entries (from src/lean_census.rs, mOMonadOS, lines 616 and 5356 —
two separate LeanFile records for FDEAsymptotic.lean at two different paths,
one under a `dumpdir_sic_lean/...` prefix and one under the real
`p4rakernel/p4ramill/...` path; the duplication itself has not been
investigated): both records report theorems: 15, sorries: 0, axioms: 0,
decide: 2, native_decide: 1, clean: 12.

